   "source": [
    "### **Explainable AI (XAI) for Credit Risk Assessment**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Name:** Tarun Singh  \n",
    "\n",
    "### Project Title & Purpose\n",
    "The purpose of this project is to build and evaluate **AI/ML models for credit risk assessment** using the **“Give Me Some Credit” Kaggle dataset** (150,000 borrower records).  \n",
    "The goal is two-fold:  \n",
    "1. Predict whether a borrower will default within 2 years (`SeriousDlqin2yrs`).  \n",
    "2. Use **Explainable AI (XAI)** techniques to understand *why* defaults occur, ensuring transparency and regulator-friendly insights.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Overview of AI/ML Techniques Used\n",
    "- **Logistic Regression**  \n",
    "  - A linear, interpretable baseline model.  \n",
    "  - Provides coefficients and odds ratios for each feature, explaining how variables like utilization, age, or delinquency affect default risk.\n",
    "\n",
    "    \n",
    "\n",
    "- **Random Forest Classifier**\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "  - A nonlinear ensemble method that captures complex interactions.  \n",
    "  - Provides stronger predictive performance and probability calibration.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "- **XAI Methods**\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "  - **Permutation Importance** → ranks feature influence.  \n",
    "  - **Partial Dependence & ICE Plots** → show how risk changes with utilization, age, and delinquencies.  \n",
    "  - **Calibration Curves** → evaluate how predicted probabilities match actual outcomes.  \n",
    "\n",
    "Together, these methods balance **accuracy** and **explainability**.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Code Functionality\n",
    "1. **Data Loading & Cleaning** → remove index column, handle missing values.  \n",
    "2. **Feature Engineering** → winsorize outliers, add new features (`Income_per_Dependent`, `MonthlyDebtProxy`, `Total_Delinquencies`).  \n",
    "3. **Model Training** → fit Logistic Regression and Random Forest pipelines.  \n",
    "4. **Model Evaluation** → ROC-AUC, PR-AUC, Brier Score, confusion matrices.  \n",
    "5. **Explainability** → feature importance, PDP/ICE, coefficients, calibration.  \n",
    "6. **Export Results** → validation set with predicted probabilities.  \n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### Instructions\n",
    "- Dependencies: `pandas`, `numpy`, `scikit-learn`, `matplotlib`, `plotly`, `streamlit` (for optional dashboard).  \n",
    "- To run:  \n",
    "  1. Place `cs-training.csv` in the working directory.  \n",
    "  2. Run the notebook sequentially from start to finish.  \n",
    "  3. (Optional) Launch the Streamlit app with:  \n",
    "     ```bash\n",
    "     streamlit run credit_xai_app.py\n",
    "     ```\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n"
   ]
  },
