    "### Feature Engineering\n",
    "In this step, we create more informative variables for credit risk modeling:  \n",
    "- **Winsorization:** clip extreme outliers in utilization, debt ratio, and income.  \n",
    "- **Income_per_Dependent:** captures financial strain relative to family size.  \n",
    "- **MonthlyDebtProxy:** translates DebtRatio × MonthlyIncome into a $ amount of monthly debt.  \n",
    "- **Total_Delinquencies:** aggregates past due counts across 30/60/90 days late.  \n",
    "\n",
    "These engineered features better capture financial behavior and improve model explainability.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "895a103b-69e3-464c-8dbe-7ff18f99f4f9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def winsorize_series(s, lower_q=0.01, upper_q=0.99):\n",
    "    lo, hi = s.quantile(lower_q), s.quantile(upper_q)\n",
    "    return s.clip(lo, hi)\n",
    "\n",
    "def safe_div(n, d):\n",
    "    d = d.replace(0, np.nan)\n",
    "    return n / d\n"
   ]
