   "source": [
    "### Train/Test Split & Pipelines\n",
    "We split the dataset into training (80%) and validation (20%) sets, stratified by the target to preserve class balance.  \n",
    "Two pipelines are created:  \n",
    "- **Logistic Regression:** scaled + imputed, interpretable baseline.  \n",
    "- **Random Forest:** imputed only, nonlinear benchmark.  \n",
    "Both use `class_weight=\"balanced\"` to address class imbalance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "d6b71b41-430e-4b91-a4ad-fa30ff1d5dd2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_train, X_valid, y_train, y_valid = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X, y, test_size=0.2, stratify=y, random_state=RANDOM_STATE\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "num_cols = X_train.columns.tolist()  # dataset is numeric; if not, we handle later\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pipelines: Logistic (scaled) & RandomForest (no scaling)\n",
    "logit_pipe = Pipeline(steps=[\n",
    "    (\"impute\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")),\n",
    "    (\"scale\", StandardScaler(with_mean=False)),  # with_mean=False robust if sparse in future\n",
    "    (\"clf\", LogisticRegression(max_iter=200, class_weight=\"balanced\", random_state=RANDOM_STATE))\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "rf_pipe = Pipeline(steps=[\n",
    "    (\"impute\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")),\n",
    "    (\"clf\", RandomForestClassifier(\n",
    "        n_estimators=300, max_depth=None, min_samples_leaf=5,\n",
    "        class_weight=\"balanced\", n_jobs=-1, random_state=RANDOM_STATE\n",
    "    ))\n",
    "])\n"
   ]
  },
