    "### Calibration Curves\n",
    "We plot calibration curves to compare predicted vs observed default probabilities.  \n",
    "This step evaluates whether the models’ predicted probabilities can be trusted as real-world risk estimates.  \n",
    "- A well-calibrated model’s curve follows the diagonal (perfect match).  \n",
    "- Miscalibrated models systematically over/underestimate risk.  \n",
    "Calibration is critical for **capital requirements and risk-based pricing**.\n"
   ]
